== SessionStart creates the session as idle, and decodes the escaped Windows transcript_path ==
start: s1 idle (created)
sessions/s1 line 1: idle <epoch>
sessions/s1 line 2: C:\Users\dev\.claude\projects\demo\s1.jsonl
sessions/s1 line 3: -
sessions/s1 line 4: <fix>/repo
== UserPromptSubmit marks it busy, rewrites lines 2-4 and registers the repo behind the cwd ==
busy: s1 busy
sessions/s1 line 1: busy <epoch>
sessions/s1 line 2: <fix>/tx/s1.jsonl
sessions/s1 line 3: -
sessions/s1 line 4: <fix>/repo
repos/<cksum>: <fix>/repo
== a second SessionStart (compact, resume) KEEPS the session — it never downgrades busy ==
start: s1 busy (kept)
== tick: one verdict pass, at most one press, and the presser word lands in daemon/last-press ==
tick: active pressed
presser side-effect: yes
daemon/last-press: pressed
== the disabled flag: the verdict is still reached and logged, the press never happens ==
tick: active disabled
daemon/last-press: disabled
== every session idle and its transcript cold: quiet, and nothing is pressed at all ==
idle: s1 idle
tick: quiet no-press
== SessionEnd forgets the session outright ==
end: s1 removed
== the registry this run built, paths normalized ==
<home>/daemon
<home>/daemon/last-press
<home>/repos
<home>/repos/<cksum>
<home>/sessions
== THE LIVE PATH: zero bytes on stdout and rc 0, for every one of the four ==
live start rc 0  live-stdout-bytes: 0
live busy  rc 0  live-stdout-bytes: 0
live idle  rc 0  live-stdout-bytes: 0
live end   rc 0  live-stdout-bytes: 0
daemon/hook.log (the live path stderr sink): present
daemon lock: absent
daemon/pid: absent
